      "side": 1,
      "message": "used_device_id_mask is read into a local but never updated, so the mask stays zero: every add writes device_id[0], and track_device_id_remove() always returns -EINVAL since it never finds a set bit. process_its_mapd() feeds that error to cwriter_write(), which stops processing on the first failing command, so I think every MAPD with V\u003d0 will stall the emulated queue and the driver will hit its completion timeout. The remove path also doesn\u0027t clear the slot on a match, so the table never drains once adds are fixed. Could you take a look? It might also be worth initializing used_device_id_mask (and tracked_pfns) explicitly in pkvm_init_gic_its_emulation() rather than trusting the contents of the host-written page at donation time.",
